# Build context filter for Dockerfile (the `vcs-mcp` container image).
#
# The build stage runs `dotnet build`/`dotnet publish` on the sources, so the context
# needs src/, tests/, benchmarks/ and the root MSBuild files — and nothing else. Two
# reasons this list matters beyond context size:
#   * a host bin/obj tree (Windows or macOS artifacts) copied into the Linux build would
#     be picked up by AssemblySearchPaths and silently mix platforms;
#   * repository/agent state (.jj, .git, .work) has no business inside an image layer.

## Build outputs — never copy host artifacts into the container build.
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
CoverageReport/
/output/
/.fsdocs/

## Version-control metadata. The image is built from a checkout's *files*; it needs no
## history. SourceLink degrades to "no repository information" rather than failing.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.jj/

## Orchestration / agent-local state and instructions (never part of a release artifact).
.work/
.claude/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

## Editor / IDE local state.
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
*.DotSettings.user

## Docker's own inputs — the daemon reads them before the context is unpacked.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

## Release-pipeline scratch (written by .github/workflows/release.yml).
release-notes.md
